t the dose of 0.1 mg, there was severe respiratory decompensation and NEC in one patient, and', 0.9925571001590566], [[[200.32553100585938, 1026.8145751953125], [1458.7239990234375, 1025.7056884765625], [1458.7239990234375, 1058.9718017578125], [200.32553100585938, 1060.0806884765625]], 'sepsis in another patient. These events are frequent in mechanically ventilated preterm infants.', 0.9954066028197607], [[[199.21875, 1094.4556884765625], [1481.9661865234375, 1097.7822265625], [1481.9661865234375, 1129.9395751953125], [199.21875, 1126.6129150390625]], 'The randomized trials of budesonide + surfactant to date (21, 24) and the observational study by', 0.9885017486910025], [[[198.1119842529297, 1135.48388671875], [1475.3255615234375, 1136.5927734375], [1475.3255615234375, 1173.185546875], [198.1119842529297, 1172.07666015625]], 'Kothe et al.(28) have not identified any major safety concerns related to the use of budesonide,', 0.9851006083190441], [[[199.21875, 1177.6209716796875], [1494.140625, 1176.5120849609375], [1494.140625, 1213.1048583984375], [199.21875, 1214.2137451171875]], 'specifically in relation to spontaneous intestinal perforation (SIP). There is however a theoretical', 0.9893597954511643], [[[201.4322967529297, 1220.866943359375], [1435.4818115234375, 1220.866943359375], [1435.4818115234375, 1254.133056640625], [201.4322967529297, 1254.133056640625]], 'safety concern in regards to SIP, for early dexamethasone treatment in a study by Stark et al.', 0.9881009465836464], [[[201.4322967529297, 1263.0040283203125], [1480.859375, 1263.0040283203125], [1480.859375, 1296.2701416015625], [201.4322967529297, 1296.2701416015625]], '(0.15 mg/kg per day x 3 days, starting within 24h of birth, then tapering over a period of 7 days:', 0.9939814368072821], [[[198.1119842529297, 1302.9234619140625], [1359.1146240234375, 1304.0322265625], [1359.1146240234375, 1337.2984619140625], [198.1119842529297, 1336.1895751953125]], 'total dose 0.89 mg/kg) was associated with SIP (13% vs. 4% in placebo; p= 0.02) (30).', 0.9924487261211171], [[[200.32553100585938, 1345.060546875], [1456.510498046875, 1345.060546875], [1456.510498046875, 1377.2177734375], [200.32553100585938, 1377.2177734375]], 'Currently, in the NICHD NRN, the incidence of SIP is 4% in extremely preterm infants (GDB', 0.9906964228394326], [[[200.32553100585938, 1384.9798583984375], [1470.8984375, 1384.9798583984375], [1470.8984375, 1421.5726318359375], [200.32553100585938, 1421.5726318359375]], 'data, 2018), ranging from 0% to 8% in different centers. However, budesonide in this proposed', 0.9937438304706286], [[[201.4322967529297, 1428.225830078125], [1372.3958740234375, 1428.225830078125], [1372.3958740234375, 1461.491943359375], [201.4322967529297, 1461.491943359375]], 'trial will be given intra-tracheally with low concentrations expected in the blood (21) as', 0.9902981347507901], [[[201.4322967529297, 1469.2540283203125], [1429.947998046875, 1469.2540283203125], [1429.947998046875, 1501.4112548828125], [201.4322967529297, 1501.4112548828125]], 'compared to systemic administration in the study of early dexamethasone by Stark et al(30).', 0.9851001939930759], [[[200.32553100585938, 1510.2822265625], [1414.453125, 1510.2822265625], [1414.453125, 1543.5484619140625], [200.32553100585938, 1543.5484619140625]], 'Therefore, SIP as a result of budesonide as used in this trial is possible (given the data with', 0.9902556551130195], [[[200.32553100585938, 1551.310546875], [1460.9375, 1551.310546875], [1460.9375, 1584.57666015625], [200.32553100585938, 1584.57666015625]], 'dexamethasone from Stark et al (3o)) but unlikely (given the data from the studies to date with', 0.9792228096409847], [[[198.1119842529297, 1591.2298583984375], [1441.015625, 1592.3387451171875], [1441.015625, 1625.6048583984375], [198.1119842529297, 1624.4959716796875]], 'budesonide+surfactant). Hence, SIP will be one of the safety outcomes that will be evaluated', 0.9930173527935277], [[[200.32553100585938, 163